{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1790790148","published":"2026-09-30T17:42:42Z","modified":"2026-11-27T16:30:13.038910705Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-19666","CVE-2026-19667","CVE-2026-80274"],"summary":"Fix CVE(s): CVE-2026-19666, CVE-2026-19667, CVE-2026-80274","details":"   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver using dns64 with break-dnssec could abort\n     on a partially excluded AAAA RRset cached with a NOQNAME proof\n     (use-after-free on the filter64 path)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19666.patch: clear the NOQNAME proof alias\n       on the DNS64 filter64 path\n     - CVE-2026-19666\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver could abort after caching a negative answer\n     of exactly 65536 bytes as a zero-length negative cache record\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19667.patch: reject negative cache records\n       that do not fit in a dns_rdata_t\n     - CVE-2026-19667\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver could abort on a wildcard answer whose\n     NOQNAME proof owner carries both a signed NSEC3 and an unsigned NSEC\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-80274.patch: record the denial type the\n       validator accepted and use it when caching and serving the NOQNAME\n       proof; adds dns_rdataset_addnoqnametype() to keep the libdns ABI\n     - CVE-2026-80274","affected":[{"package":{"name":"bind9","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bind9?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.16.50-1~deb11u6+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1790790148.json"}},{"package":{"name":"bind9-dev","ecosystem":"TuxCare:Debian:11","purl":"pkg:deb/tuxcare/bind9-dev?distro=debian-11"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:9.16.50-1~deb11u6+tuxcare.els1"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/debian11els/CLSA-2026-1790790148.json"}},{